// tests/fixtures/ambiguous_decls/cycle_direct.nv
// Phase 0 adversarial fixture: DIRECT classification cycle (A → B → A).
//
// To classify `Ping`, the resolver finds a call `Pong()` in the body.
// Determining whether `Pong` is a type or a function/macro requires
// classifying `Pong`. To classify `Pong`, the resolver finds a call `Ping()`
// in the body. Classifying `Ping` requires classifying `Pong` — cycle.
//
// This MUST produce a "declaration classification cycle" diagnostic (E0010),
// NOT infinite recursion or a silent guess.
//
// --- Why the previous version was wrong ---
// The previous fixture was:
//     Alpha: { value: Beta }
//     Beta:  { value: Alpha }
// Both bodies are field declarations (`identifier: type_expr`). Field type
// references don't require classifying the referenced declaration — they only
// look up the name as a type. Both classify independently as structs. No cycle.
// A genuine cycle requires CALL expressions whose callee classifications are
// mutually dependent.
//
// (EXECUTION_GUIDE.md Phase 0; COMPILER_ARCHITECTURE.md §4)
//
// Expected: error E0010 "declaration classification cycle" (Ping and/or Pong)
// Expected golden: tests/golden/ambiguous_decls/cycle_direct.json

Ping:
    Pong()

Pong:
    Ping()
